{"trans": "Advocate for fair competition, oppose deceit and trickery, and promote a flourishing online environment; advocate for unity and cooperation, oppose harming others for personal gain, and promote mutual benefit and win-win outcomes online."}
{"trans": "In summary, perhaps more overseas companies believe that listing in the United States is not worth the cost, so they choose to retreat as the best strategy, but this by no means indicates that they are ready to give up the U.S. market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a jittery market environment, it is extremely difficult for gold to remain unaffected, and talking about breaking the $1,000 mark is probably nothing more than a pipe dream."}
{"trans": "The police officer explained that the behavior of these students was an act of bravery. They stepped forward in the critical moment when the elderly person fell into the water, which is very commendable. It is understood that the elderly person has a mild mental illness and, after full rescue efforts by the hospital, is now out of danger."}
{"trans": "Of course, the above methods are just a limited and effective few for review. The arrangement of review and preparation should be diverse and not confined to a single approach. At the same time, it should be tailored to the unique characteristics of each candidate. Wishing all candidates a great start and great success!"}
{"trans": "It has flowed into another long river in this lifetime and this world, the place where Zhaojun dismounted. Riding on the stones of history, still speaking, the grass is as green as it was back then, and the flowers carry scents of the past. A herd of cattle and sheep does not recognize today, bowing their heads with humility and prudence. In the meticulous passage of time, drinking water remembers its source. People sit amidst the fragrance of wine, South Lake’s autumn waters, nightfall with no smoke."}
{"trans": "This belief is not about seeking to be well-fed all day, nor about pursuing longevity. Since a person cannot live twice, how can one realize the meaning and value of life before death? Even if it means being shattered into pieces, one must leave behind a resounding echo like the clear ring of jade hitting the ground and burst forth with the light of life in this world."}
{"trans": "The others were still able to remain calm, holding their guns and observing the enemy situation in all directions. However, Li Wenbin was flustered and in a panic. He dove headfirst into a clump of grass, his buttocks raised high, covering his head with both hands, looking extremely embarrassed. His companions all covered their faces and chuckled, and Li Wenbin's prestige instantly plummeted."}
{"trans": "\"How do you plan to be a king?\" the animals asked, half-believing and half-doubting. \"First, mediate disputes with impartiality, fairness, and reason. Second, handle state affairs diligently and with dedication, bearing hardships without complaint. Third, when facing powerful enemies, lead by example and charge ahead in battle. This is my inauguration speech.\""}
{"trans": "He is experienced and worldly, having gone through many ups and downs in life. Like a compass needle, he can change direction; his North Star is unpredictable and not fixed. Thanks to his pleasing sweet talk, he remains despicable yet never suffers any setbacks. Furthermore, he is eloquent and speaks incessantly (unless he isn't paid enough)."}
{"trans": "The first time I followed my colleague to the stock exchange, it was destined that I would form an unbreakable bond with stocks. Seventeen springs, summers, autumns, and winters have allowed me to experience the ups and downs of the stock market. After many ups and downs, I’ve become a veteran, and the past is vividly clear!  \n1. The sea of suffering is boundless; turn back, and there is the shore."}
{"trans": "The defeated soldiers fled for a long time before finally stopping. He looked up to the sky and sighed, \"I raised an army at the age of twenty-five, undefeated in battle, invincible in attacks. Now, in my twilight years, I have suffered such a crushing defeat. It's enough to drive me to despair!\" The victory report of the Battle of Ningyuan reached the court, and everyone in the court was overjoyed. They all raised their cups in celebration."}
{"trans": "Newlyweds are receiving a constant stream of well-wishing relatives and friends. Since the living room's decor should not be overly unique, it should prioritize comfort and warmth. It should not only make the residents feel at ease but also give guests a sense of being at home. Soft fabric sofas and cushions are indispensable elements."}
{"trans": "I said, \"Stop making analogies, let's keep the discussion focused on the issue at hand.\" My son said, \"For many years, I’ve observed your attitude indifferently and feel that you regard computers as too sacred. You don’t dare touch this, and that can’t be moved. You mothers seem to have the biggest mental block in learning, which is treating computers like a deity.\""}
{"trans": "Always on edge, afraid of saying the wrong thing, doing the wrong thing, or offending others. In the life of those with the seventh precept of sorrow, some unfortunate events often come to mind, bringing an involuntary sense of sadness. The eighth precept is suspicion — people plagued by excessive doubt always believe others are plotting against them, so every word and action must be guarded, leading to constant restlessness and frequent insomnia."}
{"trans": "In a shameful corner, there stood a pitiful guillotine, sneaky, nervous, and disgraceful, as if it were always on edge, fearing being caught red-handed while committing misdeeds—because every time it finished its work, it would immediately sneak away. How could one not feel a sense of relief at all this!"}
{"trans": "At this moment, the true allure of fighting lies in the readiness for battle after agreeing to a fight, the intense atmosphere before it begins, the sharp exchanges during mediation, the camaraderie after the dispute is settled, the unbreakable bond when meeting again in the future, and the solidarity during future fights. This cycle repeats, and the ranks of pacifists grow ever stronger."}
{"trans": "The baron's wanton insults are simply intolerable; just wait, shameless scoundrel, for the sake of honor, I will take on the responsibility of revenge. The crowd's wanton insults can only be avenged by him; even at the cost of his life, he cannot swallow his anger."}
{"trans": "It seems there won't be any arguments, no storms or upheavals; now everything is calm and peaceful. But Mom once again asked an untimely question: \"Do you want to see what I looked like when I was your age?\" The daughter's response was strange and equally untimely: \"Maybe later, dear Mom, later.\""}
{"trans": "In dealing with people and life, he is still in the preliminary stage, but when it comes to knowledge, he is full of confidence. Even the most eloquent department heads may not be more sharp or eccentric than the professors at a master's thesis defense. If you ask a woodcutter how to eat Western food, he might be at a loss, but if you ask him how to chop wood, isn't that something he can do with ease?!"}
{"trans": "\"You are about to reap the consequences of your idleness.\" After the ox finished speaking, it lowered its head back under the yoke and pulled its cart, loaded with fertilizer, away. You should live an upright and honorable life, always staying vigilant throughout your life, and never being lazy or idle. If you still feel no shame, you will surely suffer the consequences of your actions."}
{"trans": "He painted it, and painted it so vividly and lifelike. His art repeatedly fooled people's eyes, making them, at first glance, mistake it for a real object, without realizing it was a painting. For hundreds of years, the art of painting, which had always been considered lowly and vulgar, unworthy of elegance or high esteem, was revived and glorified in his hands."}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors have often been mythologized, regarded as sacred and inviolable, mysterious and unfathomable, thereby worshipped and revered as though they were deities, which is why they came to be called the \"Son of Heaven.\" In reality, emperors are also human; they have their strengths and weaknesses. Among emperors, there were wise rulers with great talents and strategies who stabilized and governed the country, as well as incompetent and mediocre rulers."}
{"trans": "Once upon a time, he \"laughed heartily and walked out the door,\" chanting, \"How could people like us be mere weeds?\" The deceit and schemes of officialdom, the hypocritical pretenses of the secular world, and the merciless reality cooled his fiery passion. How could the golden facade of a \"court-appointed literati\" ever contain your unrestrained spirit? Finally, after experiencing setbacks and pain in your career, you let it go."}
{"trans": "\"A suspicious vagabond has been harassing our territory for some time now, spreading rumors and sowing discord. You are ordered to capture this troublemaker by tomorrow and have him executed.\"  \n\"Certainly, sir,\" the police officers said before leaving.  \nThe villain, who was one-eyed, did not notice them winking at each other while answering."}
{"trans": "The American people have never regarded their national leaders as deities, nor have they blindly followed their words. However, Obama succumbed to his supporters’ expectations of him. He also believed himself to be the long-awaited savior they were looking for. The silence of the people was a harsh wake-up call for him. But that feeling of instant success was so intoxicating that it almost made him lose himself."}
{"trans": "The usually smiling Taurus man, with his thoroughly pragmatic personality, cannot tolerate betrayal from within. Don’t attempt to probe his true feelings. The steady and composed bull is content with grazing and roaming; when he smiles at you, it’s like Jesus looking at his sheep. If you don’t want to shift the scene to a Spanish bullfighting arena, witnessing rivers of blood and a tragic mess, never provoke his jealousy."}
{"trans": "Geminis wouldn't find life fun if they didn't play some tricks or use their cleverness. Don't be fooled by their seemingly carefree attitude; when situations get complicated, they will catch you off guard. While everyone else is fighting tooth and nail, they manage to reap the benefits effortlessly. Once they've successfully attracted everyone's attention, they'll make a graceful exit, playing a game of push and pull with you."}
{"trans": "In reality, being in the Eurozone and bound by the euro, it is utterly unrealistic for the Germans to try to survive alone. When the Eurozone was established, it carried the grand vision of shared prosperity. Now, with the Greek debt crisis triggering the Eurozone debt crisis, mutual losses are only to be expected. When the city gates catch fire, it affects the fish in the moat; moreover, the surroundings are already ablaze, and some places are on the verge of becoming scorched earth."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, directly investing in commodities may be the most direct and effective way to combat inflation. However, when it comes to commodity investment, what often comes to mind are some alarming stories, such as people going bankrupt from trading commodity futures or airlines suffering huge losses from crude oil hedging, among others. It seems that the risks of commodity investment are so high that they deter ordinary people."}
{"trans": "The vast sky tolerates the rampage of lightning and thunder, resulting in clear skies and gentle breezes; the expansive sea tolerates the wild fury of waves, resulting in tranquil ripples; the silent forest tolerates the cruelty of survival of the fittest, resulting in birdsong and blooming flowers. The sky, the sea, and the forest, because they understand tolerance, step back at the right time, lower themselves to accept, thereby achieving beauty and extraordinariness. Lower yourself, and the world becomes broader."}
{"trans": "Looking at the ever-changing trends of the college entrance examination (Gaokao) in recent years, what we need is to firmly grasp the new trends and directions of Gaokao question-setting, plan ahead, and move from seeing things vaguely to seeing them with complete clarity. Only then can you be well-prepared, with a metaphorical army of a million soldiers ready for the battlefield, where victories are won with ease and adversaries vanish like dust. With expert guidance turning iron into gold, the journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step; a nine-story tower is built from a heap of soil. Let this be the first step in successfully embarking on your Gaokao preparation!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate yourself is equivalent to possessing the golden key to happiness. Appreciating yourself is not being self-absorbed, it is not believing that you are superior to others, it is not indulging in self-admiration, and it is certainly not being complacent. Give yourself some confidence, gift yourself a bit of joy, and grant yourself a smile—how can happiness in life be elusive then? Make it a habit to celebrate yourself often and learn to seek a joyful state of mind."}
{"trans": "Perhaps people are gradually realizing that the internet and traditional industries are not mortal enemies in a life-or-death struggle but can instead complement each other as a \"perfect pair.\" The retail industry is gradually showing characteristics of channel integration, with increasing mutual penetration and combination of online and offline channels. At present, Taobao has launched offline stores, and traditional enterprises venturing into the internet space are as numerous as fish crossing the river. From Gome and Suning to Walmart and Carrefour, the examples are countless."}
{"trans": "In summary, the commodity market is fraught with emerging uncertainties, financial hegemony continues to manipulate the market, and the rules of the game change frequently. Against the backdrop of a global debt crisis and mixed prospects for world economic recovery, the U.S. dollar remains the most significant factor influencing the trends of bulk commodities. The economic policies of Europe and the U.S. act in tandem, while domestic regulations add fuel to the fire. The interplay between these three major factors—involving capital flows and market confidence—inevitably leads to dramatic fluctuations in the commodity market."}
{"trans": "China Red is a profound spiritual culture, a spirit unique to the Chinese people. It embodies a powerful force of self-improvement, sincerity, diligence, kindness, and resilience, representing Chinese qualities passed down through millennia with a majestic and upright character. Leading furniture enterprise Lian Tianhong conveys the essence of China Red with heartfelt passion. Adhering to a business philosophy rooted in integrity, it has taken the lead in implementing transparent workshop production, setting an industry benchmark and giving the furniture industry a refreshed look."}
{"trans": "Characteristics: In \"Journey to the West,\" Tang Sanzang is tall, graceful in demeanor, kind-hearted, and highly accomplished in Buddhist teachings. He encountered eighty-one hardships on his westward journey to obtain the scriptures, yet remained unwavering in his dedication. With the assistance of Sun Wukong, Zhu Bajie, and Sha Wujing, he endured immense challenges and eventually brought back the true scriptures. \n\nSun Wukong, whose Buddhist name is Wukong (The Pilgrim), is Tang Sanzang's senior disciple. Possessing fiery eyes with golden pupils and the ability to perform seventy-two transformations and somersault through the clouds, he is fiercely intolerant of evil, fearless in the face of adversity, and exhibits an unwavering, courageous, and heroic spirit."}
{"trans": "3. Attitude toward learning: I have my own set of experiences—\"develop a sense for problems\" and \"avoid staying up late.\" In fact, once learning becomes second nature, while it may not be effortless, it can certainly be well within your control. I do not advocate the tactic of doing an endless sea of practice problems because it's unnecessary to repeatedly work on similar types of questions. Instead, we only need to compare and reflect deeply on analogous problems, summarizing methods for solving such problems. The so-called \"sense for problems\" is similar to what we often refer to in English as a \"sense for language.\""}
{"trans": "The world's longest man-made structure - The Great Wall of China\n\nThe majestic and awe-inspiring Great Wall of China stretches across the peaks of the towering mountains in northern China, with a total length of over 6,700 kilometers. Construction began during the Spring and Autumn Period and the Warring States Period. It is a rare ancient military defense project in the history of human architecture, renowned worldwide for its long history, massive scale, and grand spirit. It has been listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site and is hailed as the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\""}
{"trans": "Because of possessing capital, one keeps a low profile; because of being outstanding and unique, one avoids the ordinary and remains low-key. Essentially, luxury goods are exceptional, even unparalleled. There can be no compromise in terms of quality or in their embodiment of fashion, and they possess impeccable superiority in both artistic and stylistic culture. Luxury goods are by no means necessities of life, but their unparalleled craftsmanship and profound brand heritage undoubtedly make them essential items in life."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt as if they were filled with lead, she still strode across the street toward the parking garage. Now, drowsy and driving alone on the fluorescent-lit concrete driveway, she felt her consciousness blur. Seventeen hours ago, when she had just parked here, there were two station wagons parked on either side, so close together that she had to squeeze awkwardly to climb out of the car. Now her old Taurus looked like an orphan, standing all alone in the eighth-floor parking area."}
{"trans": "Ten years ago, perhaps no one could have imagined that the internet could become mobile along with laptops, just as twenty years ago, people could not have imagined that phones could fit into pockets and accompany modern work and life at all times. Today, various smart devices are exuding unprecedented magic, subtly transforming the way humans live. In the next decade, in fields such as terminals, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics, it is highly likely that more disruptive innovations will emerge!"}
{"trans": "We advocate for team spirit and also admire heroic acts of selflessness in rescuing comrades, but we must ensure that we do not become a burden or liability to them, striving to avoid having our comrades take unnecessary risks to rescue us. Strict training and decisive judgment in on-site situations are absolutely necessary! Before you've experienced the battlefield, stop showing off your armchair strategies in front of us. Some things are not something you, a newly graduated student officer, can truly understand!"}
{"trans": "It’s my fault for not deeply comprehending the five-character poems of the poplar tree and the seven-character poems of my grandfather. Although I have gradually made progress in the art of \"playing dumb,\" accumulating knowledge bit by bit, I have not yet achieved complete enlightenment. Last night, my neck was bitten by a mute mosquito, and I shouted: \"How can you bite someone without making a sound? How can you suck blood without being open and upright about it? How can you fail to learn how to be a respectable mosquito, boldly roaring toward my neck?\" Therefore, I live in exhaustion and absurdity, often hearing the humming laughter of insects and mosquitoes."}
{"trans": "When barbecue stalls spring up like mushrooms after the rain in every corner of the city, people's nights become increasingly flavorful. However, it is truly difficult to enjoy both delicious food and an elegant environment at the same time. As the sun sets, painting the sky red and meeting the lush green of the sports field's lawn, tables are arranged in a staggered manner according to the terrain amidst this beautiful scenery. Barbecue chefs skillfully grill the food, waiters shuttle back and forth, and customers chat and laugh, all immersed in comfort and relaxation. Gentle music plays softly in the background, adding to the ambiance."}
{"trans": "Hearing what I said, the old gentleman let out a long sigh: \"Ah, I’ve been through near-death experiences countless times; it’s truly hard to put into words!\" Thus, this inherently proud and obstinate old man finally opened up to me—a writer who was a complete stranger to him—for the first time about his tumultuous life and inner world... In his narration, sometimes intense, sometimes heavy, sometimes with tears streaming down his face, and other times laughing heartily, I felt the profound experiences of a seventy-year-old man who had weathered countless hardships, his magnificent yet tragic life, and the inescapable manipulations of fate..."}
{"trans": "It seems that Western politics is far from as clean as people imagine. Beneath the veneer of integrity flows a muddy undercurrent, albeit with a distinctly Western flavor. Politicians openly and grandiosely \"sow the seeds\" on the surface, while \"harvesting\" reasonably and legally behind the scenes. Experienced and cunning politicians cooperate seamlessly and tacitly with shrewd capitalists. The game of mutual exchange between officials and businessmen, trading favors for money and power, is played with such sophistication that it becomes open and legal, to the extent that even Western democracy and the rule of law are powerless to address it."}
{"trans": "After wading through water for several hours, a vast cavern suddenly came into view. \"Oh my gosh, this isn't an underground cave, it's literally an underground forest!\" a team member exclaimed. The cavern was as large as a basketball court, with a ground covered in jagged rocks, gently flowing streams, and crisscrossing ravines. Stalagmites as thick as a bowl had grown over ten meters tall, accompanied by massive stone draperies, uneven stone formations, and intertwined stone columns. The surreal formations resembled a primeval forest, and with countless crystals sparkling under the glow of their lights, walking through it felt as if stepping into a fairy-tale world."}
{"trans": "The scale of the heart can shrink to be very small, only able to hold a family, a person, a sesame seed, a drop of virus. A single thread of rain can drown it. A wisp of wind can shatter it. A mere rumor can cause it unbearable pain. A single conspiracy can plunge it into eternal ruin. The heart can be very hard, harder than any known metal in the world. The heart can be very soft, like weeping silk or delicate fabric. The heart can be very resilient, enduring countless breaks and grievances, yet returning to its original smoothness. The heart can also be very fragile; a moment of carelessness can cause it to shatter like jade."}
{"trans": "Strolling within, one sees lush greenery providing ample shade, vibrant blossoms vying in beauty, and a serene, tranquil atmosphere that is utterly captivating. A gentle breeze carries a delicate fragrance, instantly bringing a sense of exhilaration and relaxation. Stone-paved winding paths lead to secluded spots, surrounded by harmoniously arranged flowers and trees, accompanied by the crisp, melodious sound of gently flowing water. Multiple layers of intertwined scenery create a vivid, lively picture of life. With each step, the view changes—every flower, leaf, blade of grass, tree, stone, and spring exudes a unique charm, drawing one away from the clamor of the world and allowing the experience of unity with nature and the cleansing beauty of the soul. Meandering through this enchanting landscape, one fully embraces the delight of existence."}
{"trans": "The furious former whaling crew said, \"This is the whale we caught.\"  \nThe smug current whaling crew said, \"Then how did it end up with us?\"  \nThe furious side said, \"It escaped again.\"  \nThe smug side said, \"Who told you not to tie it securely?\"  \nThe furious side said:"}
{"trans": "The sanctimonious appearance cannot hide your arrogance and greed! Pretentious doctors, babbling witches, glib-tongued frauds, are mocking our incompetence—watch out for the slap! You ungrateful husbands, thinking yourselves clever and capable, look down on love and kindness."}
{"trans": "A two-month-long farce has come to an end, but why Foxconn is so angry about these two reports remains unclear to us. A wealthy and powerful company is not short of think tanks, and crisis management tactics can include not only emotional appeals but also high-profile anger: perhaps as a warning to others, or perhaps as a diversion."}
{"trans": "Reward and confer ranks based on merit. Delicious food and fine flavors should belong to it. \"I see you as pitiful and ridiculous, so arrogant and conceited,\" the wild duck replied, \"Your perspective is biased. We wild ducks fly across the skies, free and unrestrained, making our home wherever we go. Yet you depend on others; we earn our living, while you beg for food from others.\""}
{"trans": "The opening of an article is the most challenging; it must be abrupt and vigorous, straight to the point, and hit the nail on the head to captivate readers. There’s no need to beat around the bush or use cliched phrases. He also told me that when reasoning becomes entangled and complex, introducing an analogy can effortlessly resolve all the convoluted arguments—how economical and skillful that is! Thoughts like these..."}
{"trans": "She solemnly began to perform divination. After a flurry of activity, she pretended to examine the sand tray and made some calculations. Then she raised her head, looked at Kudi, and said, \"You despicable scoundrel! How dare you speak nonsense in front of me! The divination clearly states that your name is Kudi, and you are a bandit who murders, robs, commits all sorts of atrocities, and is utterly depraved.\""}
{"trans": "The castle was indeed like a paradise isolated from the world. He gazed at the magnificent building, his heart filled with awe and admiration. They strolled through the garden, picking fresh fruits to eat, and were utterly enchanted by the atmosphere of birdsong and fragrant flowers, completely reluctant to leave. By the time they leisurely finished exploring the entire castle, night had fallen. They returned to the hall by the pool, planning to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The air conditioning is indeed quite effective. The cool, fresh air, the orderly layout, the impeccably dressed guests, and the polite waitstaff—all of these make the place feel like a wonderland, exceptionally comfortable. It is always people who spoil the atmosphere. Those impeccably dressed gentlemen eat with oily, shiny faces, making it uncomfortable to watch. They all nod at Nikolai, and for some reason, some even wink at him."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to waver. Seeing that they were facing a dead end and that the tide had turned against them, they finally abandoned resistance and fled into the city. The armored trains continued to move back and forth, sweeping away the remaining enemies. They were like two majestic land dragons pressing forward triumphantly, crushing everything in their path. They leveled the enemy's fortifications where they had hidden and sent the slower-running enemies to their demise. They were a soul-stirring declaration of victory by the Chinese army, proclaiming the end of the stubborn invaders."}
{"trans": "After this calamity, our family never recovered, the family estate declined, and we fell into poverty and destitution, struggling amidst hunger and cold. The old locust tree lost its former glory as well; the remaining half of the tree stump stood solitary and desolate, lonely in the semi-barren courtyard, exposed to the wind and rain, enduring the chill of dew and frost. For many years, it languished without vitality, neither sprouting new buds nor growing branches, and entirely ignored by others, leaving it to \"stand\" upright, \"sighing toward the heavens.\""}
{"trans": "Anything reactionary is bound to collapse if you don’t fight it. Dust doesn’t disappear by itself unless the broom sweeps it away. You’re all doomed, only I, Zhang Pujing, a loyal Bolshevik, stand upright with integrity, untainted by corruption – righteous in every sense. Hahaha, revolution is not like inviting someone to a banquet, writing an essay, painting, embroidering, or frying dough sticks. The proletariat will completely suppress all of you monsters and demons."}
{"trans": "Excessively glorifying top scorers in college entrance exams can make them feel superior to others. Some may develop a sense of complacency, arrogance, and self-centeredness, unconsciously lowering their standards for themselves in future work and life, becoming stagnant and resistant to collaboration with others. Alternatively, some might believe they must never fall behind others, excessively pursuing perfection, acting cautiously, overthinking, hesitating, and strictly adhering to rules. All these factors can lead former top scorers to lack creativity and passion in their actions, ultimately making it difficult for them to achieve great success."}
{"trans": "I will treat each of my patients equally, regardless of whether their clothes are luxurious or tattered, whether their appearance is handsome or unattractive, whether they are wealthy or in poverty, whether their status is high or low, whether they are immaculate or covered in sores, whether they have a serious illness or a minor ailment, whether they are polite or rude to me, whether they are well-cultured or uneducated, whether they are humorous and witty or dull and expressionless, whether they are dignitaries or ordinary people..."}
{"trans": "Love is free. That involuntary admiration, that uncontrollable longing, that deep affection in weathering storms together, that devoted love in mutual support, is the most profound solace and the firmest reliance in life. And all of this is free, something money cannot buy. Goals are free. Whether you are a prince in luxurious attire or a destitute wanderer, as long as you are willing, you can set a goal for your life. This goal can be great or ordinary, splendid or simple. As long as you are willing, you can have it."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your goals, you should focus your energy, plan the path to success, and then move forward with all your might. During this process, you cannot be indecisive, distracted, or easily swayed. At the same time, you must rigorously eliminate doubt and fear, as they will undermine your determination, disrupt your emotional drive to move forward, and impact your efforts to fully achieve your goals. Those whose hearts are filled with doubt and fear will ultimately accomplish nothing and gain nothing. When doubt and fear infiltrate your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all strong thoughts will be severely shaken and completely collapse."}
{"trans": "An educated person holds profound respect, reverence, and admiration for various noble qualities of humanity, such as loyalty, courage, trust, diligence, mutual support, self-sacrifice to save others, fearlessness in the face of danger, perseverance through hardship, and unwavering integrity. Not everyone can necessarily embody all of these virtues, but they understand how to cherish and praise them. It is acceptable for people to feel fear or laziness, but they must not disguise these shortcomings as lofty virtues, nor should they denigrate those who uphold such noble qualities as hypocrites simply because they themselves cannot achieve them. You may kneel in the mud, but you must not smear the mud across the chest of the entire world and then make a show of declaring that there is filth everywhere."}
{"trans": "This world has beginnings that are silent and unnoticed, beginnings that are grand and dramatic, beginnings that are cautious and meticulous, beginnings that are bold and decisive, beginnings that are hidden and secretive, beginnings that are half-hearted and reluctant, beginnings with ulterior motives, and beginnings that are honest and open. Every stage of life, every event in life, is approached differently by different people, each giving their own unique way of beginning. These approaches reflect a person's mindset, vision, courage, demeanor, and magnanimity in managing their life."}
{"trans": "Generally speaking, the final stage of review plays a crucial role in the entire preparation process. Therefore, we must place great importance on the review during the final stage, while avoiding mistakes that could render previous efforts futile and cost us the chance of success. Below are explanations of a few common pitfalls."}
{"trans": "Currently, the stock market lacks clear leadership, with major sectors taking turns to adjust and inadequate efforts to stabilize the market. This makes it very challenging for mainstream funds to operate, leaving the market weak and jittery, like a startled bird. Any negative news causes a panic response, leading to intensified panic selling. Meanwhile, funds on the sidelines remain in a wait-and-see mode. Additionally, with the holiday approaching, the willingness to go long is not strong, further dispersing market sentiment."}
{"trans": "The Japanese, who were stubbornly resisting, were already barely holding on. Their barely maintained front lines were like a warship riddled with holes, leaking from all sides. Once dealt this fatal blow, it immediately shattered like a weathered rock. In fact, stopping the armored train from advancing was not difficult; simply dismantling the tracks in advance would have sufficed."}
{"trans": "Fish Eyes Mixed with Pearls: How to Distinguish Between Authentic and Fake?  \nHandheld walnuts are becoming increasingly recognized and loved by people, causing market prices to rise significantly. At the same time, counterfeit products created with high-tech methods have become widespread. In the beginning, Old Hu was also deceived, but now, he has gained plenty of experience and knowledge. He even holds onto his walnuts while sleeping at night, making it nearly impossible to fool him anymore. He has shared some tips with the Evening News readers on how to identify the authenticity of walnuts."}
{"trans": "In my life, I have been much like others, walking on both wide roads and narrow single-plank bridges. Through ups and downs, twists and turns, I have made my way. I cannot deny that I have been quite lucky; the successes I’ve achieved and the hollow fame I’ve gained are somewhat undeserved. On the other hand, my misfortunes have also been beyond what ordinary people might experience. During the horrifying so-called \"Great Revolution,\" I nearly lost my life for daring to speak out for righteousness. The physical suffering I endured is also unforgettable for a lifetime."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang can be regarded as one of the greatest strategists in Chinese history. In Longzhong, he compared himself to Guan Zhong—what confidence that was! His prediction of the division of the land into three kingdoms was remarkably accurate! When he first emerged onto the scene, he faced Xiahou Dun’s army of 100,000 without fear; at Bowang Po, he set fire to the battleground, earning the admiration of Guan Yu and Zhang Fei; at Xinye, he burned the city, striking terror into Cao Ren; his ingenious stratagems outwitted Zhou Yu three times, showcasing his intelligence with a touch of humor; he remained loyal, refusing to declare himself emperor even with Liu Bei’s permission; and faced with a desperate situation due to a strategic miscalculation, he implemented the Empty Fort Strategy, demonstrating an extraordinary composure that commands respect. However, what moves me the most is not any of these, but rather the poignant scene of the \"Autumn Breeze at Wuzhang Plains.\""}
{"trans": "When night falls in the mountain village, we can hear the sharp barks of dogs rising and falling in waves. After midnight, the barking becomes faint and intermittent, and the lights at the windows light up one after another, like pale faces resembling cabbage hearts… The moonlight, too, washes its face by the water pipes in the courtyard…"}
{"trans": "A close-range shot, missed; a header in front of the goal, unexplainably off target; even a one-on-one chance, unable to seize the opportunity... The lack of training opportunities in domestic leagues has made the U20 national team's ability to capitalize on chances in the attacking front lamentable. This is also the biggest flaw of the current U20 national team."}
{"trans": "But in the sociological sense, the Palestinians and Israelis of today are irreconcilable enemies. The reasons lie both in the fact that after the Jewish diaspora from Palestine in 556 BCE, the two brothers were separated across the world, unable to meet for over a thousand years, leading to estrangement, indifference, suspicion, and hostility; and in the fact that two thousand years later, the Jewish people returned to Palestine to establish the state of Israel. As a result, their mutual struggles turned into slaughter, and the bond of brotherhood completely dissolved."}
{"trans": "National policies descended from above, causing a sharp downturn in the industry's situation. Ceramic production areas bore the brunt, resembling trapped beasts in a predicament. The production areas are struggling, and ceramic enterprises are searching for a way forward. As the cold wave strikes, while it brings impact and pain to the production areas, it also enables them to more clearly see the path ahead. Detailed reading: The industry's situation has plummeted, and many ceramic production areas are struggling like trapped beasts."}
{"trans": "Entering Su Garden, wandering through the courtyard of Suzhou, one might see small bridges over flowing water, white walls with black tiles, winding paths leading to secluded spots, or unexpected turns revealing new vistas. The most profound impression is that its meticulously crafted garden-building process echoes the Imperial Gardens of the Forbidden City. The arrangement of corridors, pavilions, and waterside pavilions is layered and well-proportioned, creating the illusion that walking along a mere 20-meter path feels as if traversing 3 to 5 miles with broad and expansive views, evoking the sensation of being in a painting."}
{"trans": "The situation on the battlefield is ever-changing, and since ancient times, there have been no fixed rules for winning a war. Decisions such as how to arrange troops, deploy forces, whether to attack or defend, whether to engage in positional warfare or mobile warfare, whether to voluntarily abandon or hold a stronghold, which areas to give up and which to hold steadfastly—these should all be determined by the frontline commander. The supreme commander should avoid excessive interference. In fact, any strategy or tactic can be comprehended and applied flexibly; it is hard to say which method is superior. This is the idea that \"all roads lead to Rome.\" Ultimately, victory is the most important principle."}
{"trans": "A novel is the backlight of the soul. By injecting a part of your soul into your work, you give it your flesh and blood, thereby elevating it to the heights of art. This involves two issues: First, a writer needs to examine the true state of their own soul and shape themselves first. Second, the power of sincerity is immense. The meaning of sincerity here is not only to correct excesses but also to discard the trends of artificiality, sycophancy, sensationalism, and opportunism in creation. Do not scratch where it doesn't itch, do not make unnecessary moves, and do not treat sincerity as a cheap adhesive to sell. I believe sincerity should be an attitude toward life, especially for writers."}
{"trans": "The locust tree outside the window, weathered and battered by the elements, stands motionless as the unwavering moon hangs on its still branches like a bell, yet so far from the sound of a chime. I know that anything insignificant cannot be expected to land with weighty resonance. However, it is precisely this faint, fragment-like moonlight that makes the silent midnight even more like a sunken ship in the depths of the night."}
{"trans": "Cruel and ruthless, cold and unfeeling, cunning and insidious, yet I am kind-hearted, benevolent, and dedicated to saving all beings. In the eerie mansion of Dis, my soul inscribes charms and symbols with great concentration. Suddenly, the painful voice of Dulcinea of Toboso reaches me, and I come to know that she has unfortunately been struck by magic."}
{"trans": "There is suspicion of \"burning bridges after crossing the river.\" Internet analyst Xu Dandan believes that Alibaba exhibits such suspicion. \"Capital has its inherent nature, and prioritizing shareholder interests is perfectly natural. Taking on investment means accepting the terms of the capital contract. One cannot revere it as a deity when in need and criticize it as a demon when it becomes an obstacle.\""}
{"trans": "The keen and perceptive eyes are also helpless! Eyes dazzled, not daring to look directly at the throne. We come from the East, but the events occurred in the West; the procession is both vast and long — its beginning and end cannot be seen. Falling forward and advancing after, scrambling to get ahead, courage surging, spears in hand, one fighting against ten, ten against a hundred, millions of lives vanish without a trace."}
{"trans": "Seizing Zubailu, he was overjoyed and smug. But when he left home for a trip, upon his return, he learned from his family that Zubailu, along with a bag of gold and silver at home, had vanished without a trace. Upon hearing this news, he flew into a rage, huffing and glaring, berating and hitting himself, even tearing the clothes on his body. The more he thought about all his efforts coming to nothing, the angrier he became."}
{"trans": "2008, an extraordinary year. In the battlefield of public relations and marketing for domestic enterprises, it could be described as turbulent and full of strife. For companies' market public relations personnel, it seemed that \"PR crises\" struck like a ferocious flood overnight, causing fear and trepidation. Time flies forward swiftly, and in the blink of an eye, 2009 is approaching. Looking back on this year, many business owners may still feel lingering fear, treading cautiously."}
{"trans": "Leo friends almost never refuse tasks at work. As long as it gives them a chance to showcase their talents and abilities, they will grit their teeth and help. However, this also makes it easy for them to forget things, and the accumulated workload can be quite significant. Therefore, keeping a calendar and a weekly planner on hand is the most suitable tool for improving workplace productivity. Especially those with a lively and playful design, as it matches their childlike nature, allowing them to tackle challenges effortlessly even when they're busy."}
{"trans": "An excellent composition should include six or seven refined sentences: first, vivid and beautiful metaphorical sentences; second, grand and magnificent parallel sentences; third, emotionally rich personification sentences; fourth, profound and allusive sentences; fifth, thought-provoking philosophical sentences; sixth, complementary contrasting sentences; and seventh, lively and poetic sentences. Skillful use of these refined sentences makes the writing concise yet meaningful, with profound implications and highlights that enhance the entire piece, making each sentence worth ten and naturally increasing its literary brilliance."}
{"trans": "What is even more ridiculous is that nowadays, Western countries are still struggling economically, their money printing machines are itching to start, and their finances are already stretched thin, yet they are looking to China to \"feed\" the world... Everyone now turns their gaze to China, the world's second-largest economy. If the global system dominated by the U.S. after the Cold War is now on its last legs, will this emerging economic superpower step up? Or will it let the West reap the consequences of its own actions? However, this time China may be willing but unable to help!"}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, reigned for fifty-four years, expanding the territory to form a vast domain stretching from Liaodong and central Korea in the east, to the vicinity of Lake Balkhash in the west, to the heartlands of Vietnam in the south, and to the Sayin Mountains in Outer Mongolia in the north. The population under his rule reached nearly sixty million. Objectively speaking, among the hundreds of emperors in Chinese history, those capable of territorial expansion like Emperor Wu of Han are truly rare. Most others were fortunate enough simply to maintain their inheritance without becoming disgraced rulers who squandered the nation's dignity. In this sense alone, Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, can be regarded as a ruler of extraordinary vision and capability."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the trivialities of ordinary people's lives, lacking dramatic twists and turns in the plot, but they offer a refreshing experience due to their uniquely original perspective and undeniable personal inclinations. He excels at creating distinctive and individualized characters, which is precisely a hallmark of a genius writer."}
{"trans": "Some people bluff, pull rank, and claim to be the best in the industry or the first of their kind to create selling points, packaging themselves, tirelessly promoting and selling themselves in the sea of information. Others adopt a mindset of keeping a low profile, focusing only on themselves, biding their time, working quietly without saying a word."}
{"trans": "In reality, why do \"war of words\" always dominate the scene and persist for months without abating? What forces are fueling it behind the scenes? What exactly is subtly influencing the judgments and thoughts of internet users? Not only ordinary internet users but even some website administrators are perplexed by this."}
{"trans": "In the evening, he spread out the manuscript paper and prepared to write an essay to earn back that 20 yuan. That night, the title of his essay was: \"On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality?\" He wrote: \"In an era of fallen material desires, we must raise the banner of morality to oppose the enslavement of materialism.\" That night, his essay surged forward with a lofty tone, filled with intense indignation, sorrowful lamentation, heartfelt persuasion, fervent passion, soul-stirring cries, profound sincerity, fierce unruliness, fluent elegance, and unrestrained eloquence…"}
{"trans": "1. Argumentative essays should have a broad and far-reaching perspective. As an official-style article, the most basic characteristic of an argumentative essay is that its central idea and theme should be elevated. Writing an argumentative essay requires a focus on long-term interests, the ability to see the essence through the phenomenon, being adept at addressing matters from a high-level perspective, and excelling in elevating the theme. In other words, the written article must have a lofty ideological realm, and it must never pander to vulgarity, much less be crude, lowbrow, or full of complaints."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is compassion shown to those in pain. When he smiles, his smile is like the longing of those exploring the unknown, like the stardust that gently falls onto a child's eyelids, and also like a piece of bread in the throat."}
{"trans": "If you look further up, her shoulders are so well-proportioned! Like twin lambs, or like two jade peaks; slender like autumn hills, smooth like autumn waters. Above the shoulders lies the face that has been praised in songs and poetry."}
{"trans": "Even the lotus has the tragedy of punishing nine generations. The lotuses are connected, and the thousand fingers of the lotus petals grasped one summer and then let another summer go. Now it is the ghostly rain of an autumn night, pouring down on the water's surface covered with broken duckweed, like a disheveled, blind Chopin tormenting a piano with a thousand keys."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen under the moon deepens the meaning; discussing swordsmanship under the moon makes the spirit more genuine; talking poetry under the moon enhances the charm; conversing with a beauty under the moon strengthens the affection.  \nThe way to appreciate the moon: when it is bright, gaze upward; when it is hazy, look downward.  \nThe spring breeze is like wine; the summer breeze is like tea; the autumn breeze is like smoke; the winter breeze is like ginger and mustard."}
{"trans": "He rode on waves of blood, steering a small red boat, gracefully arriving at this damp and cold world. His final leap was propelled out of the gate of life by surging waves of heat, like silt sweeping away during a flood burst. The baby's ecstatic cries were like the smashing of glass cups colliding."}
{"trans": "If China were to gain another melancholy writer, this north-facing study should be responsible. Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a southern fruit refrigerated in a freezer. During the day, I seem to be immersed at the bottom of the ocean, where a quiet and dark gray music plays."}
{"trans": "The red candle has a spirit. She does not begrudge her life, yet she is particularly attached to it. Whenever she is about to burn out, the scorched wick unexpectedly arches high in the flame, spasmodically and determinedly upright, like the spine of a warrior suddenly hit by a bullet, solidifying midair into a sculpture of defiance, before falling heavily into a crimson pool of blood..."}
{"trans": "Step outside and look to the sky, the heavens have their order and act as a self-check; after the morning dew and rain, the sun appears, silver beads adorn everything, radiating light together, one sun giving birth to countless suns. In the corner of the wall, there is an old cobweb that need not be swept away; let the dust settle. Over time, the thread grows thick, like the roots of an old tree coiling, forming a three-dimensional mural. One can read tradition, read modernity, and with each reading, it feels ever fresh."}
{"trans": "Spring always knocks first on the bamboo gate of the garden, then lights up last year's extinguished torches, bundle by bundle. At this moment, winter, left alone in the empty house, is like a desolate wolf, fleeing in disarray amidst the suddenly arriving flames. The flames leave its lonely gaze unsettled, and the floral skirt of the earth leaves it lost."}
{"trans": "The methods used to punish evil are more evil than the evil itself; indiscriminate killing of innocents is as easy as cutting down chives. Under the banner of loyalty, filial piety, integrity, and righteousness, there are flashes of swords and blades everywhere; the price of grandeur and righteousness is a land strewn with corpses. The fundamental value of life is just a few blades of withered grass under the hooves of horses; the survival rights of the people are merely a few bubbles at the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "——Heavenly sounds, infinite mystery, the infinite encircling the finite, or the stern yet gentle command of God. Music is the omniscient and omnipotent God of notes; it is both the Creator—who arranges and determines the positions of the notes—and the Savior—if the notes can listen and follow that unceasing, unwavering resonance."}
{"trans": "The winding lotus pond is covered with endless leaves. The leaves rise high above the water, like the skirts of graceful dancing girls. Among the layers of leaves, a few white flowers are scattered, some blooming gracefully, some shyly budding; they are like scattered pearls, like stars in the blue sky, like beauties just out of a bath."}
{"trans": "Therefore, in terms of a city, if everything encountered and seen is youthful and dazzling, it must mean the timing is not yet right, the strings and zithers not yet in harmony. It is like writing: when adjectives are like a woman in heavy makeup, and parallel sentences are like lovers walking side by side, it means the essence of the article has not yet been reached. The pinnacle of writing is like an old street with sparse parasol trees, old seats beneath the trees, casual chats among the seats, refined yet unhurried."}
{"trans": "The suffering of one family does not affect the happiness of the world. Summer arrives uncontrollably, and the silk tree flowers, like pink powder puffs, brush against the lonely and desolate windowsill of the hospital ward. The girl's head has become a polygon; the long-healed bone seams, like cracked earth, stretch into black holes beneath the thin skin, as an inner demon expands in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I seem like a fruit from the south, chilled in the refrigerator. During the day, I feel as though immersed in the depths of the sea, where a tranquil gloom plays its gray music. At night, I seem to hear the sound of Eskimos' sleds gliding, while the long beard of the North Star hangs down, jingling, striking the clusters of white stalactites."}
{"trans": "They are as quiet as the bright moon, unwilling to disturb anyone, yet they undeniably disturb a large area around them. This can truly be described as \"the moon emerges, startling the mountain birds.\" Compared to Tao Yuanming's tranquility, Wang Wei's calmness carries a touch more of aristocratic elegance and refined design. His brilliance lies in being nobler than commoners yet appearing more ordinary than them, and in his designs appearing to surpass nature itself in naturalness."}
{"trans": "Even the brown coffee table is painted with emotion, a gentle little rectangle, bearing all the bustling activities on top of it. There is also a larger one, featuring white magnolias, thin and bright, somewhat like jade and crystal, reminiscent of the cool taste of a jade fish held in Yang Guifei's mouth when she suffered from a toothache. The bold strokes of the forsythia bloom and close with strength, its control over life is both leisurely and domineering."}
{"trans": "Vast and boundless, returning to that great wilderness!\" Reading this passage, it doesn't evoke sadness in me but rather a sense of beauty, the kind of feeling akin to reading in *Records of the Grand Historian* about Jing Ke crossing the Yi River in white robes to assassinate the King of Qin, full of vivid imagery. Imagine, a young master from a wealthy family, seeing through worldly affairs, shaving his head, barefoot, dressed in a red cloak, bidding farewell to his father in the snow—how beautiful that is!"}
{"trans": "We cannot bypass that dark, humiliating, and indifferent Chengde era, just as we cannot avoid facing the ugly and desolate Taoist Tower when approaching the Mogao Caves. No matter how splendid and magnificent Dunhuang is in our memory, it can never fill the emptiness of the Sutra Cave, cannot wash away the pallor in the Thousand Buddha Caves, and cannot heal the blood-stained scars of the ancient peoples on the horizon."}
{"trans": "Oblivion visits us more and more frequently, becoming an unwavering friend until death. I use this friend as a filter—what is forgotten is no longer necessary to remember, and the subconscious controls memory, like the wind commanding a kite on an invisible plane. The new, sharp threads weave an uneven net of memory as a filter, and what remains congealed is like cheese, sweet yet containing hard lumps that hurt the teeth."}
{"trans": "His chest was broad and upright, containing the earth-shattering roar of ancestors chasing wild beasts. His pelvis dipped sharply inward, with prominently raised bones indicating the former attachment of powerful muscles, like the ropes of boat trackers on the Yellow River, pulling the entire body in a gecko-like ascent. And his limbs, like the long and graceful tusks of an African elephant, emitted a smooth, jade-like glow."}
{"trans": "It was only years later that I dispelled my lingering resentment and admitted that day was a steep turning point in my life. What prompted me to discard the painting of withered roses was not the art teacher's ridicule, but seeing your talent shine so brightly and brilliantly that I broke my own paintbrush with a gesture of regret. What is regret like? It's like a tiny mole on your body, one whose location and emergence only you are aware of."}
{"trans": "I comb my hair on the balcony, shedding like falling leaves, hair drifting down in waves, brushing against my arms, like night rain. In the distance and nearby, many car horns blare anxiously; the darkening sky spreads out in all directions, like a lake of boundless mist and clouds. Across the way, from a window on the lowest floor of a building, rises a wisp of pale white smoke, hesitating as it ascends, as if uncertain where the sky is."}
{"trans": "She carried a kettle in each hand, and it reminded me of a woman gathering her spirit while walking on a thin rope. It was all because of her waist; her waist, her waist was so soft—like Bai Shui would say, so soft that it felt like eating Suzhou’s sticky caramel candy. Not just her waist, as I wrote in my diary: she possesses a set of curves that rival the beauty of clouds and the brilliance of the moon, weaving a vast and mesmerizing net!"}
{"trans": "Because of your language, you fall silent, and when you sink to the deepest depths, you let yourself disappear. Losing language, thereby losing the self, losing the entity of existence, Yang Lian thus realized he had become a \"ghost.\" A ghost, floating between cities, watching coldly (like an insect, a ghost is also an \"it,\" only able to observe), observing the complete annihilation of \"meaning.\" There is the sea, but the port holds no meaning for you."}
{"trans": "A streetlamp and another streetlamp are far apart, and between segments of brightness lies segments of darkness. My shadow sometimes appears in the brightness, sometimes disappears into the darkness. The wind that arises out of nowhere stirs the colorful fallen leaves wave after wave, as if evoking impressions of life. I feel like this empty wind, only able to perceive my existence when the colorful fallen leaves are swept down and spun up."}
{"trans": "However, as we stood on the open land—my father, brother, relatives, and many villagers who had spilled sweat and blood, endured the scorching sun, and braved the wind and rain—we listened to the distant sound of thunder and stood motionless. No one seemed inclined to go inside to avoid the northwestern rain. Our hearts were heavier than the dry sky, and everyone remained silent, for our hearts were also a rain-filled sky. This inner rain seemed even more tragic and more overwhelming than the northwestern rain."}
{"trans": "Imagine, if Tang Bohu and Qianlong were both considered \"top-tier poets of ancient China,\" then we could only quietly consign the entire \"Complete Tang Poems\" to flames. The same goes for calligraphy: an astonishingly high price thrown at a piece of mediocre brushwork is like a heap of gold crushing the balance of Chinese calligraphy history. Faced with this situation, I once sighed deeply: \"When the cultural lineage is obscured, small hills are called peaks; with strong wings gone, tattered feathers pass for rocs.\""}
{"trans": "The attack came very suddenly, as if the girl had received a decree from the heavens, abruptly convulsing without any warning. The once soft and delicate girl curled up like a rigid trembling rod, every muscle shining as if made of iron. Her small body arched like a drawn bow, bouncing on the snow-white hospital bed. Countless beads of sweat dripped down from this bizarre human arch, falling drop by drop like melting snow from eaves in the warmth of spring."}
{"trans": "This released power is lonely yet strong, conforming to and breaking norms, imbued with intoxication and poetry, akin to the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. With this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu wielded his brush like a staggering drunken step, swaying and staggering, dancing with hands and feet, exuding elegance and vitality as all his movements flowed seamlessly into one. Then, he would throw down his cup with a laugh and fall into a deep sleep. Zhang Xu did not realize that his drunken steps were also the very steps of Tang Dynasty culture."}
{"trans": "But just as I held my breath and concentrated intently on listening, suddenly, all at once, they all fell silent. The cicadas startled me again! Like a piece of string, the cicada's song had tightly bound my heart, and then, without any warning, it loosened the knot. As a result, my heart, unprepared, scattered, like a wave leaping towards the sky, only to accidentally crash onto the sand! I hadn't even realized when summer had crossed the threshold and entered!"}
{"trans": "I once shed tears in sorrow for your humiliation and frustration.  \nMy tears ran like streams, clear as crystal, yet unable to wash away your thick layer of filth, only removing the obstruction from my eyes.  \nThese tears could not dampen your hearts of iron and stone in the slightest, only extinguishing the flames of anxiety and eagerness within me.  \nNow, in the face of your suffering, I laugh. This laugh echoes like thunder; it does not come after the storm but resounds before it."}
{"trans": "I gradually understood that when facing disaster, one cannot use the grammar of disaster. There is another kind of grammar that directly leads to a poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From this point on, the state of my life was no longer the same. Every time I read Zhuangzi's chapters such as \"Autumn Floods,\" \"Free and Easy Wandering,\" \"Discussion on Making All Things Equal,\" and \"In the World,\" it feels like looking at electrocardiograms closely related to me. With such a philosopher who feels overly close, I find it difficult to make calm and impartial assessments, and thus I can only keep a certain distance."}
{"trans": "You press your forehead against the embroidered patterns of gold threads. When the sun was on this side, it made the gold threads scorching hot, but now they have cooled. The people of the past struggled through their lives, and what they did gradually became covered in dust; when descendants hang out clothes, they shake off the dust again, making it dance in the golden sunlight. If memories had a scent, it would be the fragrance of camphor—sweet and steady, like the distinct recollection of happiness, sweet yet sorrowful, like forgotten sorrows."}
{"trans": "It is precisely this extent that brings them closer to life, allowing us to still feel close to them even thousands of years later. The liveliness of Yang Guifei, I imagine, is like a ceramic soup pot, warm and jade-like, sitting at one's feet. As the water inside gradually cools, it gives off a gentle and tender warmth. Su Qing, on the other hand, is like a small red clay stove, with its own independent fire. You can see the bright crimson flames and hear the crackling sounds of chestnuts bursting, but it is relatively harder to tend to—it requires adding coal and wood, and the smoke can sting your eyes."}
{"trans": "Like surging waves or raging tides, it strikes against the emotions buried deep in your heart. In an instant, you feel that the sound of the cicadas, like fierce waves washing over the sand, snatches away the light melancholy tightly held in your hand. The urgent cries of the cicadas abruptly halt at the climax of their melody, like a beautiful piece of prose suddenly torn apart, scattering sonorous words all around, falling like the sound of metal and stone. Then, silence ensues, becoming a fragmented and incomplete passage, leaving behind only some melancholy and sorrow. Is this not the song of life?"}
{"trans": "Here lies vibrant youth, burning hearts of fiery red, no dispirited little old men, only robust \"old young people.\"  \nThe silver-white moon lingers in the vast, empty sky, as if shedding tears, hating its own solitude...  \nAnd then there is the swimming pool, always like a kind old granny, smiling with a face full of wrinkles. When she sees many lively children leaping into the water like little mermaids with splashes and thuds, she is so happy that she bursts into great silver sprays."}
{"trans": "For thousands of years, it has been a lost wasteland. On the other side of the wasteland are vague and unnamed great craftsmen, while on this side of the wasteland is a panicked modern woman. On both sides, kilns burn fiercely, like two beacon towers separated by vast mountains and rivers, yet the signals relayed between the beacon towers are accurate without fail. Most other beacon towers are related to war, but only these two are not. Across the bloodshed of the Three Kingdoms, the struggles of the Sui and Tang dynasties, and the battles of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing dynasties, there are only two wisps of the purest, cleanest smoke, echoing each other from afar."}
{"trans": "Lin Daiyu's brokenness lies in her profound and unforgettable love; Sanmao's brokenness stems from a moment of clarity and transcendence after enduring life's hardships; Van Gogh's brokenness is caused by the sun using golden knives to inflict constant pain in the light; Beethoven's brokenness is the collision of the most spiritual black and white keys, composing a tragic and magnificent symphony of life. If the brokenness of ordinary people reveals the purest and most beautiful light of humanity, then the brokenness of these exceptional souls is like silvery fireworks filling the sky above our heads."}
{"trans": "The face is washed several times a day, yet it still isn't clean; the eyes are never washed in a lifetime, yet they are always bright. The empty space cannot fulfill the function of a mop or broom, so there's no need to spend money on it. After all, people are mobile; they are naturally dust-repellent. Strangely, the air doesn’t become thin due to the confined space. To observe the act of breathing, one replaces the invisible air with the visible form of cigarette smoke—inhale once, exhale three times. The curling smoke rises to the ceiling, forming a canopy of auspicious clouds; one may first glance downward to observe the abundance of species, then gaze upward to admire the vastness of the universe."}
{"trans": "To know oneself but not to know others is merely a way of staying confined in a corner, growing old and dying without ever interacting with others; it is no different from summer insects that cannot discuss ice, frogs at the bottom of a well, or donkeys in a mill. Only by being able to understand others can one truly have self-awareness; just like the fan of Princess Iron Fan, it must be able to open in order to close. The more one knows, the broader the connections; scattering oneself across the world, immersing oneself in everything and every matter, observing their size and shape, weight and density—only then can one analyze even the tiniest details and gradually, gradually recognize one’s true self."}
{"trans": "The singing is like drifting clouds and flowing water, relieving worries and allowing one to wander within. It is also like surging waves and roaring tides, striking the emotions settled deep in your heart. In an instant, you feel as if the sound of cicadas, like fierce waves sifting through sand, has swept away the light sorrow tightly clutched in your hands. The urgency of the cicada's sound abruptly halts at its highest note, resembling a splendid article suddenly torn apart, scattering powerful and resonant words like the sound of metal striking stone. Then it falls into silence, leaving only fragmented remnants, and leaving behind a sense of melancholy and sorrow."}
{"trans": "What is there to be nothingness? The matters of gods are unknown to humans; human matters, even amidst the confinement of fate—one could even say helplessly—construct and continue meaning, thereby redeeming the present and also eternity. Therefore, \"eternal recurrence\" is by no means \"a complete affirmation of earthly life,\" but merely states that humans cannot escape earthly life, not even in death. As for affirmation, it points to the pursuit and transcendence of eternity, that is, the earth's gaze toward the heavens—that grand music has always filled both heaven and earth."}
{"trans": "Viewing Master Xiaoyun's Zen paintings offers a completely different experience. The feeling is as if we are reading the pastoral poems of Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei late at night. With just a few simple strokes and light touches of ink, it does not stir up overwhelming emotions in the heart; instead, it quiets our restless spirit. It does not fill our hearts with something, but rather washes away the mundane concerns that originally cluttered them. It is like a mountain stream after a torrential rain—initially turbid, but as the rain clears and the sky brightens, the stream becomes crystal clear, and the mud and filth in the mountains are entirely cleansed away."}
{"trans": "The sound is sometimes slow, sometimes fast, sometimes high, sometimes low, sometimes loud, sometimes deep, sometimes intermittent, sometimes continuous. At times, it is like the ring of metal and jade, at times like the resonating tones of a large bell, at times like large and small pearls falling onto a jade plate, at times like red coral and white coral sinking into the sea, at times like playing a plain zither, at times like dancing amidst lightning, at times like the chorus of a hundred birds, at times like a rabbit caught by a hawk. My imagination runs wild, I cannot contain myself, my heart overflows with joy, and the inspiration flows freely from my pen. The dead words seem to come alive, and I too seem to brim with youthful energy. Rarely in my life have I experienced such a state of mind, something that is difficult to describe to others."}
{"trans": "Perhaps the clouds are meant to roam in the sky, unlike the sun with its fiery wheel-like feet, and so they won’t descend to accept my fervent kindness. It’s merely my illusion. However, this illusion is simply too beautiful. If the blue sky is an unwritten book of heaven, then clouds must be the unwritten annotations, and the swift trails of my car translating the language of the clouds onto the road become the latest published commentaries. The sky narrates with ever-changing blue hues, the clouds depict with clean strokes, and then hand it over to my eyes to print. Together, we are recounting the story of Kuafu."}
{"trans": "I found it inconvenient to take it out and eat on the plane. When I returned to the United States and had a taste, it was overly greasy and too spicy—nothing like the sausage rolls my father occasionally made for me. Back in Shanghai, right next door to our house was the Qi Shi Lin Café, which had relocated from wartime Tianjin. Every day at dawn, they baked bread, setting off an olfactory alarm. A burst of fragrant, overwhelming aroma pierced the air with the momentum of a strong wind sweeping thousands of miles, yet it was also the gentlest kind of alarm clock. However, it always went off at the wrong time, rudely waking people up, leaving one helpless, much like a bothersome spring scene that cannot be avoided. Having this \"fragrant\" neighbor was truly a type of disturbance."}
{"trans": "Happiness in life is like the sugar cube used to coax a child into taking medicine, or more like the mechanical rabbit used to lure greyhounds into racing at the track. A few minutes or days of happiness make us feel that a lifetime of enduring much suffering is worth it. We hope for it to come, hope for it to stay, hope for it to come again — these three phrases sum up the entire history of human effort. While we pursue and wait, life subtly slips away without us noticing. Perhaps we are merely the chips consumed by time, and living a lifetime simply serves as a burial offering for those years, without any real thought of happiness."}
{"trans": "There is a type of dark silk with a greenish hue, over which large black shadows sweep, full of the energy of wind and thunder. Then there is a kind of Japanese silk fabric, a pale lake color, shimmering with wood grain and water patterns; at regular intervals, two plum blossoms the size of teacups float on the water, their designs resembling iron strokes with silver hooks, much like the stained-glass windows of medieval chapels, with heavy iron-edged borders embedded in red glass. The most common fabrics in the market are those bearing colors that are hard to name—neither quite green, gray, nor yellow—only suitable as backgrounds. These are neutral tones, also called protective colors, civilized colors, or blended colors."}
{"trans": "This comes from her movements; her every step, every stretch of her waist, every brush of her hair, every glance, every lowering of her head, even the slight flutter of her garment and the gentle sway of her skirt, all flow like honey and ripple like a breeze. How could we not rejoice and marvel at such beauty? The most charming of all is her soft, supple waist; people used to compare it to the willow’s gentle sway in the wind, or to the water-snake waist of Qingwen in *Dream of the Red Chamber*, praising the slim and supple nature of the figure. But the waist I adore is, in fact, like Suzhou's cowhide candies, filling my tongue with sweetness and my teeth with softness. With such a soft waist, her hands and feet naturally carry an extraordinary grace."}
{"trans": "Next to me, there were some crookedly leaning wine bottles, with not much wine left in them. It’s a pity that I don’t drink; otherwise, at a time like this, taking a sip or two would surely be the finest enjoyment. “Raising a cup to invite the bright moon,” the moon would shyly dive into your cup. A gentle breeze passes by, and you can hear the rustling of the forests on the mountains on both sides. Amid the swaying branches, the lights become even more flickering, like mischievous children playing hide-and-seek with you. Combined with the shimmering light dancing on the river’s surface, it feels as if they’re playing together in a harmonious symphony. What kind of earthly dreamscape is this?"}
{"trans": "I can no longer explain it clearly. On the stage, under the real sunlight, how could there be such a sense of desolation? There is a place overlapping between art and reality, making things hazy; like holding a matchstick burning in the sunlight, flickering faintly, barely visible with its pale orange-yellow flame, but making one more acutely aware that even one's hand in the sunlight is but a temporary thing... On the stage, the maid sang for a while, held a tea tray, moved through rooms and doorways with a grace like parting flowers and brushing willows, stepping over countless thresholds, entered the study, made a deep bow to the young master, and raised the tea tray high to the level of her brows."}
{"trans": "I saw a calico cat lying lazily under a section of crumbling, abandoned wall. Morning glory flowers bloomed in a lush mix of green and vibrant purple, as the cat stretched its body nonchalantly.  \n\nIn the hazy night, I saw the streetlight casting the shadow of a transformer box onto a white construction wall by the sidewalk, mingling with the intertwining shadows of swaying street trees. It looked just like the balcony where Romeo serenaded Juliet with a love song.  \n\nI saw the face of the poet Zhou Mengdie framed perfectly in a small window of a moving bus as I waved goodbye to him. It was as if the entire bus, with great solemnity, was serving as a frame for him."}
{"trans": "You long for that pure, childlike heart full of desire yet loving everything, but you can see it lingering in the faint morning mist, no matter how you wave your hand at it, it never returns to your chest. How \"lacking\" this feels! So, Mr. Pingbo, feeling somewhat stifled, simply and gently, like the soft breeze of spring whispering among the green trees, softly and closely shares with you his memorable yet ungraspable \"childhood.\" Although he cannot stay long in that \"childhood,\" if he can invite a few more companions to wander there a few times, it might slightly alleviate his sense of emptiness, and that taste of melancholy may no longer cling persistently at the root of his tongue."}
{"trans": "You can also say that it is the starting point for Chinese people moving towards modernity. However, which other nation's path to modernity has been as hasty, flustered, timid, and chaotic as it was in Shanghai? You could also say that it is a city civilization rising up in defiance of agricultural civilization. Yet, is there any other urban civilization that has been so deeply overshadowed, fragmented, encircled, and enveloped by the immense forces of the countryside as Shanghai has? In short, it is a grand paradox: when you focus on its filth, it will rise with dazzling brilliance; when you worship its great power, it will turn around and show you the scarred and battered back wall."}
{"trans": "However, the truth is quite the opposite. I sat there quietly, listening to the sound of raindrops above me. At this moment, sound triumphs over silence, and I felt an immense joy in my heart, as if I had drunk celestial nectar or absorbed divine essence, with a sense of transcendent euphoria. The sound was sometimes slow, sometimes urgent, sometimes high, sometimes low, sometimes loud, sometimes soft, sometimes continuous, sometimes intermittent. At times, it was like the resonant clash of gold and jade; at times, like the deep tones of great bells; at times, like large and small pearls dropping onto a jade plate; at times, like red coral and white jade sinking into the sea; at times, like playing a lute string; at times, like a fierce, thunderous dance; at times, like the chorus of a hundred birds; and at times, like the swift motion of a falling rabbit pursued by a falcon. My imagination ran wild, completely beyond control, and joy blossomed in my heart, inspiring words to flow freely from my brush."}
{"trans": "Surrounded by numerous flashy billboards and shops, car horns honking incessantly; he was like the person from ancient legendary tales who dreamt of the ephemeral yellow millet dream, except he merely woke up from a nap without having such a dream—there was an added sense of pity. ... The Taoist walked to the front of a hardware store, prostrated himself, of course, they didn’t give him any money, and he seemed indifferent to everyone, bowing blankly and then moving on. He got up, \"tok—tok—\" tapping as he transitioned to the doorway of the tobacco shop next door, where he once again \"knelt in the dust,\" tilting his head sideways. His movements resembled a dark, stagnating flow, like a black chrysanthemum slowly blooming."}
{"trans": "What does it matter? Birds chirp in spring, crickets cry in autumn, mosquitoes buzz like thunder in summer; at night, insects wake while birds sleep. Wind and rain are not constant, and when no one arrives, dogs do not bark, nor do hens cackle without laying eggs. Only humans use language, actions, or machines to produce sounds anytime and anywhere. Even when alone in a room with no one to interact with, a person might play a phonograph, listen to the radio, or even emit thunderous snores during sleep. Language, of course, is not just sound. However, in unpleasant, unwanted, or distant conversations muffled by walls or space, words lose their edges and contours, becoming a swelling and shrinking cacophony, as meaningless as the crowing of roosters or the barking of dogs."}
{"trans": "As time goes by, the past is forever gone and cannot be turned back to the moment when one first met the peach blossoms. However, in human memory, the charm or lingering wounds of the past often surge back like waves crashing ashore, making the present an extension of that charm or those wounds, continuing further and regenerating. If life were a blank book, pre-bound and pre-numbered, the disturbances of past affections to a person would be like writing on a page with too much force, causing the ink stains to seep through the subsequent pages, indelible. Of course, there is no need to destroy old pages for momentary relief, just as there is no need to demolish the Yellow Crane Tower once the crane has flown away. Yet, spreading out the old history under the light, proceeding where one should and stopping where one must, remains necessary."}
{"trans": "The Great Northwest is a basalt mountain where not a single blade of grass grows, a vast desert with solitary smoke rising straight. You, studying geology, carry a large canvas geological satchel on your shoulder. You have been on the road for twenty years.  \n\nTwenty years of living in tents, in the sand dunes and seas of sand, like a small boat. The cold crescent moon shines down. The chime of Hanshan Temple outside Suzhou—can it \"reach a traveler's boat at midnight\"?  \n\nYour wife, that beautiful woman, is gazing at you. The web of longing covers her face as she tries to salvage a distant heart of love.  \n\nYou return home once a year. Each time, you plant a cluster of bamboo by the door. But then, you leave again, leaving her only the word \"individual\" formed by the bamboo leaves."}
{"trans": "If life were a blank book pre-bound and pre-numbered, the disturbances of past experiences on a person would be like writing too heavily on one page, causing the ink to seep through to the subsequent pages, leaving indelible marks. Of course, there is no need to destroy the old pages to feel relieved, just as there is no need to tear down the Yellow Crane Tower simply because the yellow crane has flown away. However, under the lamp, spreading out the old history, proceeding where one should and halting where one must, is indeed necessary. After embracing life in its entirety, when looking at old events or new matters, one can regard them with tolerance and generosity, granting them the positions and meanings they deserve. If it is something beautiful, one can discern what kind of new branches sprout from the buds of this event; if it is something saddening, one can also see a tender branch stretching upward from a gloomy day into a sunny one."}
{"trans": "Everything feels distant from me, even my own shadow in the bright moonlight appears more hazy than mist. Just as I thought of turning around to sleep, for some reason, my steps hesitated for a moment. Suddenly, the fleeting remnants of a dream paused momentarily, though they quickly flew off again like an arrow released."}
{"trans": "The final hope is merely an aesthetic support. Like a shipwreck in the icy sea with no chance of rescue, looking up to glimpse the scene of rolling dark clouds; like facing certain death under a flurry of blades, glancing down to see the splattered patterns of blood. Aesthetic support is the final support."}
{"trans": "What we gather from the past and the future are merely seeds.  \nWhen you are a wish wandering in the mist, I wander there as well.  \nWe search for each other, and from our longing, dreams grow.  \nThose dreams continue endlessly, those dreams stretch infinitely."}
{"trans": "In such purity, the dish is oneself, the person cooking is oneself, and the person eating is also oneself. Just as love is oneself, the one who knows this love is oneself, and the one who remembers this love is also oneself. One tastes oneself bite by bite, and across the cup of time, one intoxicates oneself."}
{"trans": "The long pants clung tightly, making it impossible to take a step. The heart was as pure as a blank sheet of paper, as void as a newborn baby. Saying farewell to the sea, bidding goodbye to a lonely seabird circling in the sky, I will return to speak of the dust of the vast earth and distant heavens. Picking up the umbrella and shoes, picking up all the myriad things of the human world."}
{"trans": "Unpredictable. I only hope that, even if it is a human flaw, it should present itself in a proper manner. Like the furrowed brows and deep sighs of a noble warrior, rather than the chaotic midnight brawls of a group of ragged soldiers; like the millennia-long standoff between two snowy peaks, rather than a tangle of wild vines twisting around a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night, the plateau was extraordinarily beautiful. The sky seemed like a blue artifact fired during the Jingtai era of the Ming Dynasty, deep and boundless. Even through the silver table-like immense moon, the metallic blue light behind the moon could still be seen. The moonlight couldn't rival the tint of the blue sky, and it lingered faintly like diluted ink, thread by thread."}
{"trans": "Watching the same movie repeatedly is like spitting out food you've eaten and chewing it again. In that moment, the top of our heads turned golden, as if covered in wheat awns. I recall a character in Gorky's book once said that lovers from youth should not meet again later in life, as if a skeleton had risen from the ground..."}
{"trans": "When I close my eyes, I think of it; when I open my eyes, I need it. Yet when it all comes rushing toward me, almost drowning me, I suddenly don’t even know what I truly want. I only feel my heart aching relentlessly, as if tightly bound by silken threads, as if scorched by falling drops of candle wax, as if tossed about on a vast and desolate sea."}
{"trans": "The faintest echo of your sobs will become its voice. \"After life is veiled, it is concealed and hidden, just like the greatest of your souls. When life speaks, all the winds turn into words; when life speaks again, the smile on your lips and the tears in your eyes will also become words.\""}
{"trans": "As a result, the collective cultural personality gradually dimmed. Seasons passed, plum blossoms withered, and cranes aged; culture became a purposeless waste, and the pursuit of closed-off moral perfection led to overall immorality. The advance of civilization was thus canceled, leaving behind a pile of plum petals and crane feathers, like bookmarks tucked into the annals of the national spirit."}
{"trans": "Using science and philosophy as the standard to grant a pass to religious spirit is like using intellect and reasoning to engage in love—it suppresses the passion of life and drains love of its charm. Replacing religious spirit with political and economic policies is like treating family background and wealth as conditions for marriage, turning children into reproductive machines and making them spiritual eunuchs."}
{"trans": "In fact, all destruction is concrete, all grievances are difficult to articulate, and therefore those answers are also questionable. What should not be doubted is the result—withered grass and rubble bearing the weight of disasters throughout history. I am willing to face all this in a perilous situation without any protective mechanism, like removing gloves to touch the scars of the elderly."}
{"trans": "Now, I have written so many pages. I see myself as a child, copying a passage from a long hymn; a hymn the angels sang when God created the first human. Perhaps I am like an illiterate person, memorizing a sentence from a book written by wisdom; a book that was inscribed on the first page of emotions before time began."}
{"trans": "Even if it is a major event spanning millennia, even if it is a great feat connecting thousands of miles, if it belongs to culture, it is often borne on a pair of aged shoulders. Like smugglers, like fugitives, evading along the way, making secret inquiries, searching for a place of trust. The decision to entrust is always written in a will, and thus it is destined to be impossible to explain the cultural significance of one's life while alive."}
{"trans": "There is no need to doubt the results: withered grass and rubble carry the weight of disasters from ancient times to the present. I am willing to face it all in a perilous situation devoid of any protective mechanism, like removing gloves to touch the wounds of the elderly. This touch often provokes deep reflection: as the foundation of our life, Chinese civilization is also scarred, yet how has it avoided complete collapse?"}
{"trans": "Is there anyone who can deliver a ready-made meaning tucked inside your birth certificate? Birth itself is about demanding meaning from the one being born, requiring you to seek or create meaning. It's like a publishing contract with an advance payment of royalties, with a lifetime deadline. Of course, you're not the creditor; you're the debtor. Life is asking meaning from you, so there's no room for you to complain about anyone."}
{"trans": "The uneven ink, the red-inked headlines, the crossed-out names, the rows of exclamation marks, the cautious appeals, the repeated edits—all combine into a terrifying sound that rushes toward us. It’s as if just a few strands of white hair on a cobweb in the corner of a room, or half a piece of torn cloth caught among the withered leaves on a treetop, can instantly bring us back to that era we dare not think of again."}
{"trans": "Some fall on the bun of the vegetable-picking woman, some stick to the swallow's black coat, and some slide into the stream to play in the water. The river, like a thousand flute-playing wanderers, accompanies the songs of children leaving school. When mischievous children place their books on their yellow straw hats, carry their shoes in hand, and wade through the river, will the spore babies pop out of the flute holes, bite the children's clothes, and finally return to the soil of their wild fern mother?"}
{"trans": "Soul, return and go back to your old home.  \nWhen he spoke Minnan dialect and caused people to laugh out loud, when he spoke Beijing dialect and left people looking at each other in confusion, why did he never defend himself: here, his Chu dialect was as profound as the heavens, the earth, the mountains, and rivers, as grand as the skies and spirits?  \nEvery tone of the master of ceremonies was like the tone of his father reciting \"Chen Qing Biao\"—mournful and sorrowful, every tone struck you deeply."}
{"trans": "He was too thin; his withered skin couldn't fill the gaps between his ribs, and his chest was like a steel bridge, stretched across his ribcage. His violent and dull heartbeat resembled a blood-dripping sun, burning hollowly, emitting sounds of flames and caverns. Mei Ying had heard Yue Beizhi's heartbeat before—deep and resonant, beating steadily and rhythmically through his well-developed muscles, like coal buried deep within the earth's crust."}
{"trans": "From one inn to another, never settling in a mountain village or by the water's edge, what talisman is there that I could pray for? Perhaps it is youth, but how fleeting it is. I am like someone who has unearthed a treasure, carrying pearls, gold, and silver in a flawed mesh bag, only to realize that it grows lighter and lighter along the way, as youth scatters into dust. Perhaps it is scriptures and classics, but how can a mind full of knowledge restore the broken mirror in my hands?"}
{"trans": "On the mountain slope of his hometown, when greeting from afar, it is definitely not the soft and drawn-out \"Hey——\" of city folks, nor the feigned surprise \"Wow——\" of southerners. The \"hey\" and \"wow\" cannot travel far and would be swallowed up by the mountains. Only the deep, resonant, long-lasting, and desolate \"Uh-ha——\" can soar like a hawk for a long time. Now, this hawk-like cry descends from the sky like mist, and an endless homesickness, both hot and spicy, fills Shen Zhanping's chest."}
{"trans": "Hurry to escape the political quagmire that you don’t even fully understand, and pursue the long-lost poetic sentiments. Pursuing poetic sentiments is also pursuing the self—the self once familiar to the whole land, the self once held tightly by the embrace of a wife, the self believed to have been found but instead was lost. This time, in turning back to chase it, there is the morning glow to see you off, the river flow as witness, the cries of apes giving encouragement, and countless mountains making way. Thus, the boat of life, once burdened ever heavier, transforms back into a light skiff."}
{"trans": "Although airplanes can be likened to Zhuangzi's carefree wanderings or Liezi's wind-riding journeys, they are not as captivating. Unlike the long-distance trains with their hypnotic rhythms and ever-changing scenery, which, when viewed through the window, seem both worldly and otherworldly at the same time. Thus, when traveling abroad, wherever the clanging double tracks reach, I always stand on the platform—truly a \"long pavilion\"—waiting for the train, with its vigorous beauty and rumbling momentum, to pull into the station and carry me to distant places."}
{"trans": "Confronting prominence is normalcy, confronting the officialdom are the common people. More concealed than the dense grass and trees in the mountains is the normal everyday life of ordinary people disappearing into a small town. Concealment in the mountains still retains and boasts a kind of aloofness, but aloof concealment is ultimately insincere; on the other hand, concealment in small-town streets not only avoids deliberately tormenting or destroying life but also allows life to be lived very comfortably, letting existence settle in tranquil yet convenient corners, almost dissolving itself from the inside out, thus becoming the highest form of concealment. Perhaps calling it concealment is too narrow; anyway, in my heart, flowing streams over small bridges, serene households, and sentiments of nostalgia for simple pleasures all represent an ecological image of a religious philosophy of life."}
{"trans": "The spring breeze does not recognize me; why does it enter the silk curtains?"}
{"trans": "Henceforth, no heart to cherish the fine nights, let the bright moon descend behind the western tower."}
{"trans": "The candle has a heart and still cherishes farewells, shedding tears for others until dawn."}
{"trans": "Chang'e must regret stealing the elixir, her heart longs every night under the blue seas and clear skies."}
{"trans": "Thrice seeking advice for the realm's plans, twice assisting the court with a loyal minister's heart."}
{"trans": "Three kingdoms divided plan and scheme, a single feather in the clouds for eternity."}
{"trans": "A song of \"Hou Ting Hua,\" so mournful it is unbearable to hear."}
{"trans": "The swallows that once perched in the halls of the Wang and Xie families now fly into the homes of ordinary people."}
{"trans": "Melancholy arises with no way to see Fan Li; staggered misty trees lie to the east of the Five Lakes."}
{"trans": "If the east wind does not favor Zhou Yu, the two Qiao sisters would be locked away in the deep spring of the Bronze Sparrow Terrace."}
{"trans": "Victory and defeat are the affairs of soldiers and are unpredictable; enduring shame and humiliation is the mark of a man."}
{"trans": "How could being an emperor for four reigns compare to the Lu family having Mo Chou?"}
{"trans": "The jade ornament bids farewell to the phoenix palace, iron cavalry surrounds the dragon city."}
{"trans": "Why should the Qiang flute resent the willow? The spring breeze does not cross the Jade Gate Pass."}
{"trans": "Amidst a hundred battles in the yellow sands, clad in golden armor,  \nI shall not return until Loulan is conquered."}
{"trans": "The bright moon of the Qin era and the frontier passes of the Han era, after the long journey of thousands of miles, the soldiers have not yet returned."}
{"trans": "The frontier traveler gazes at the border hues, longing to return home with much sorrow on his face."}
{"trans": "Shoot the horse before shooting the man, capture the leader before capturing the bandits."}
{"trans": "The vast sea stretches with a railing of hundred-foot ice, melancholy clouds darken and freeze for ten thousand miles."}
{"trans": "The forest is dark, the grass startled by the wind; the general draws his bow at night."}
{"trans": "The vast desert's sand is like snow, and the moon over Yan Mountains resembles a hook."}
{"trans": "At noon, hoeing the crops under the blazing sun,  \nSweat drips onto the soil beneath the crops."}
{"trans": "A single rider brings a smile to the imperial consort, unaware it's lychees that have arrived."}
{"trans": "Fine horses and luxurious furs,  \nCall the boy to trade them for fine wine,  \nLet us together dispel the sorrow of eternity."}
{"trans": "Desiring to cross the Yellow River, ice blocks the stream;  \nAbout to climb the Taihang Mountains, snow covers the peaks."}
{"trans": "The emperor calls, but I refuse to board the boat; I proclaim myself the immortal of wine."}
{"trans": "Nature bestows divine beauty, dividing dusk and dawn with the interplay of yin and yang."}
{"trans": "I possess no enchanting charms; a rooster's crow turns the whole world bright."}
{"trans": "I reflect on the vastness of heaven and earth, feeling solitary and desolate, tears streaming down."}
{"trans": "Endless falling leaves rustle down, the unending Yangtze River flows and surges forth."}
{"trans": "The spring breeze brings joy, and the horse gallops swiftly; in one day, all the flowers of Chang'an are admired."}
{"trans": "Zhuang Zhou dreamed of butterflies, lost in the illusion; Wangdi entrusted his spring longing to the cuckoo."}
{"trans": "The vast desert sees solitary smoke straight,  \nThe long river reflects a round setting sun."}
{"trans": "Sitting alone in a secluded bamboo grove, playing the zither and letting out long, drawn-out sighs."}
{"trans": "The waterfall plunges straight down three thousand feet; it seems as if the Milky Way is descending from the heavens."}
{"trans": "The window frames the snow of Mount Xiling from a thousand autumns,  \nThe door anchors boats from distant Eastern Wu."}
{"trans": "The riotous flowers gradually become dazzling to the eyes, while the shallow grass is just enough to cover the horse's hooves."}
{"trans": "The four hundred eighty temples of the Southern Dynasties, how many pavilions and towers are shrouded in mist and rain."}
{"trans": "During the Qingming Festival, drizzling rain falls, and travelers on the road are grief-stricken."}
{"trans": "I wonder who cut out the fine leaves; the spring wind in February is like scissors."}
{"trans": "In April when all flowers have faded in the human world, peach blossoms in the mountain temple begin to bloom."}
{"trans": "If you have a close friend living afar, distance cannot keep you apart."}
{"trans": "If friends and relatives from Luoyang ask about me,  \nTell them my heart is as pure as crystal ice in a jade pot."}
{"trans": "I urge you to drink another cup of wine, for beyond Yang Pass, there are no old friends."}
{"trans": "I send my sorrowful heart with the bright moon, to follow you all the way to the west of Yelang."}
{"trans": "The Peach Blossom Pool is a thousand feet deep, but not as deep as Wang Lun's feelings when he bid me farewell."}
{"trans": "A lone sail fades into the distance in the boundless blue sky; all that is seen is the Yangtze River flowing to the horizon."}
{"trans": "The bamboo grove temple is vast, the faint sound of the evening bell echoes."}
{"trans": "The closer I get to home, the more apprehensive I feel, and I dare not ask the newcomers."}
{"trans": "In this nocturne, I hear the sound of willows being broken; who would not feel longing for their hometown?"}
{"trans": "Beacons of war blaze for three months, a letter from home is worth ten thousand pieces of gold."}
{"trans": "Who says a tiny blade of grass can repay the warmth of the spring sun?"}
{"trans": "The sound of the flute lingers among the reeds, white birds suddenly startle and fly in rows."}
{"trans": "The tide-rider stands at the crest of the waves, holding the red flag without it getting wet."}
{"trans": "Lush and countless, roads in all directions."}
{"trans": "The light chill of dawn lingers beyond the green willows' mist; the red apricot branches burst with the lively spirit of spring."}
{"trans": "Staying overnight on the halfway fragrant grass path, still cold with signs of rain in the late spring sky."}
{"trans": "In the late night, the wind gently slows the arrival of the fragrance, not expecting that by morning, the southern branches would be in full bloom."}
{"trans": "Why seek light green or deep red colors? It is naturally the finest among all flowers."}
{"trans": "If trees had feelings, they wouldn't stay so lush and green!"}
{"trans": "The moonlight is cold, and parasol leaves drift yellow."}
{"trans": "I often recall the time of parting, on Jingshu Tower, where the bright moon resembled water."}
{"trans": "At the stillness of nightfall, just as I wish to return, there is only a river with a bright moon and jade-green clarity."}
{"trans": "Dreams break of the homeland's mountains and rivers, separated by layers of mist and water."}
{"trans": "The ribbon tied with a heart knot is not yet completed, and the tide at the riverbank has already subsided."}
{"trans": "I think back over and over, a thousand miles of misty waves, evening haze deepens, the vast Chu sky."}
{"trans": "Tearful eyes question the flowers, but the flowers remain silent; scattered petals drift past the swings."}
{"trans": "Fallen flowers, a person stands alone; in the light rain, swallows fly in pairs."}
{"trans": "A solitary grave a thousand miles away, with no place to speak of desolation."}
{"trans": "Day after day, I think of you but cannot see you; we both drink from the waters of the Yangtze River."}
{"trans": "The mountain oath remains, but the brocade letter is hard to entrust."}
{"trans": "The old affairs of the Six Dynasties flow away with the water, but cold mist and withered grass remain vividly green."}
{"trans": "With a feather fan and a silk kerchief, amid casual talk and laughter, the enemy's ships are reduced to ashes."}
{"trans": "At night, hearing the cries of a few cranes, it is said that the royal army is approaching."}
{"trans": "One should bear a son like Sun Zhongmou!"}
{"trans": "Thirty years of achievements turn to dust, eight thousand miles of journey under clouds and moon."}
{"trans": "Under the shrine of Foli, a scene of divine crows and festive drums."}
{"trans": "Drunkenly returning, leaning on the sword against the west wind, the river waves still embolden one's spirit."}
{"trans": "The river flows like a rushing whale, the mountains resemble a crouching tiger, and this natural barrier is not man-made."}
{"trans": "The mist obscures the towers, the moon confuses the crossing at the ferry."}
{"trans": "The Qiang flute plays in the clear weather, water songs drift through the night, and the cheerful fishing old man and lotus girl have fun."}
{"trans": "Amid the fragrance of rice flowers, we talk of a bountiful year and listen to the chorus of frogs."}
{"trans": "A century's rise and fall passes briefly, yet with you, I still face the same moon of that time."}
{"trans": "Helplessly, the flowers fall and fade; seemingly familiar, the swallows return."}
{"trans": "At the foot of the mountain, orchid buds barely dip into the stream;  \nOn the pine-lined sandy path, clean and free of mud;  \nIn the rustling evening rain, a cuckoo cries."}
{"trans": "The parasol trees, accompanied by fine rain, at dusk, drip by drip."}
{"trans": "Swallows fly over, asking where spring is, only the pond remains green."}
{"trans": "I wish to ride the wind and return, yet I fear the jade towers in the celestial palace, where the heights might be too cold to bear."}
{"trans": "Clearly, it was a dream of Huaxu; turning back, the east wind leaves tears all over my clothes."}
{"trans": "The vast autumn sky of Chu stretches for a thousand miles, the waters follow the sky into the endless autumn."}
{"trans": "Red beans grow in the southern country; how many sprout as spring arrives?"}
{"trans": "The sun rises in the east and rain falls in the west; it seems to lack clarity, yet there is clarity."}
{"trans": "At the place of parting by Xie Pavilion, the scenery always evokes sorrow."}
